        kind: 'worked',
        text: 'A cloud MES must send work orders to the lines and get counts back. (The simpler case, a historian copy in the DMZ for a report, is in IT fundamentals, lesson “Why the OT network stands apart”.)\n\nStep 1, function (ISA-95): orders and counts are level-3 work. Step 2, network (Purdue): the MES sits beyond level 5, the machines at levels 1 and 2. Step 3: no connection started from outside may reach the plant network. Step 4: a small MES connector at level 3 opens a connection outwards to a relay in the industrial DMZ at level 3.5, which talks to the cloud; orders come in over that connection. Step 5: record both maps in the design.',
