        text: 'Order: 1,000 caps, bill of materials 25 grams of granulate per cap. Made: 960 good, 40 scrap.\n\nStep 1: the MES confirms 960 good, but the 40 scrap is left out. Step 2: the ERP books a goods receipt of 960 caps. Step 3: backflush on the confirmed quantity books out 960 × 25 g = 24 kg of granulate. Step 4: really used is 1,000 × 25 g = 25 kg, because the scrap also took material. Step 5: after this order the ERP shows 1 kg of granulate too much. Fix: confirm the scrap too, so backflush calculates with the total quantity, or book the scrap separately as consumption.',
