        ask: 'Explain both differences: PLC against MES, and MES against ERP. Which difference calls for action?',
        reveal: 'PLC against MES: 10,240 − 10,160 = 80 cycles. That fits test cycles at the shift changes, which the PLC counts and the MES does not see as product. Check the number of changes times the test cycles per change.\n\nMES against ERP: 9,980 − 9,700 = 280 good parts. That fits Sunday’s night shift not yet confirmed. If it is in the ERP by Monday afternoon, everything is explained. If the difference is still there then, the interface is failing silently and the interface owner must find out why.',
